  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: cxf-rt-rs-security-oauth2 4.2.2.rhlw-00008",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released org.apache.cxf:cxf-rt-rs-security-oauth2 4.2.2.rhlw-00008 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-57818, CVE-2026-61466, CVE-2026-63687, and CVE-2026-68079.\n\nCVE-2026-57818: Apache CXF: OAuth2 Authorization Code Replay via TOCTOU in JCacheCodeDataProvider\n\nCVE-2026-61466: Apache CXF: OAuth2 Dynamic Client Registration Scope Self-Escalation\n\nCVE-2026-63687: Apache CXF: JwtRequestCodeFilter silently overrides outer PKCE and nonce parameters\n\nCVE-2026-68079: Apache CXF: DefaultEncryptingCodeDataProvider allows unlimited authorization code replay\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for org.apache.cxf:cxf-rt-rs-security-oauth2 4.2.2 from Maven Central.",
